\title{Plonkish Arithmetisation}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    Gate constraints plus a wiring argument, with lookups bolted on. "Plonkish" is used loosely across implementations, so the term needs a precise statement of what it covers.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{Gate constraints and selectors; custom gates and what raising the degree costs.}
        \li{Copy constraints via a [permutation argument](dhsorens-002X) — the mechanism that distinguishes Plonkish from AIR.}
        \li{Lookup tables in the halo2 sense: regions, fixed columns, and the developer-facing cost model.}
        \li{Preprocessing: what is fixed at setup and what varies per instance.}
        \li{Where Plonkish and [AIR](dhsorens-002U) genuinely differ, once cross-table lookups are available to both.}
    }
}
